<%#
  STUB — Phase 2: OnThisDayEntry model will provide today's entries
  via OnThisDayEntry.where(month: today.month, day: today.day, jurisdiction: philly)
  MVP shows static placeholder content matching the mockup exactly.
%>
<section class="section-anchor" id="otd" style="margin-top:0;">
  <div class="section-eyebrow">★ <%= @today.strftime("%A · %B %-d, %Y") %></div>
  <div class="section-heading">On this day in Philadelphia</div>
  <div class="gilt-rule"></div>

  <div class="otd-row">
    <div class="otd-feature">
      <div class="otd-date-flag">May 11 · 1880</div>
      <div class="otd-title">The Free Library of Philadelphia is founded</div>
      <div class="otd-body">Dr. William Pepper convinces City Councils to charter a free public library — one of the first in the United States. Pepper's argument anchored the idea that <em style="font-family:'Libre Baskerville',serif;font-style:italic;color:var(--gilt-lt);">knowledge belongs to the commons</em>. The Parkway Central building wouldn't open until 1927.</div>
      <div class="otd-quote">"A library is the people's university." — William Pepper, 1880</div>
    </div>
    <div class="otd-born">
      <div class="otd-born-label">★ Born today · Philadelphia</div>
      <div class="otd-born-name">Marian Anderson</div>
      <div class="otd-born-year">1897 · South Philadelphia</div>
      <div class="otd-born-body">Contralto and civil rights pioneer. In 1939, after the DAR refused her Constitution Hall, she sang from the steps of the Lincoln Memorial to 75,000 people. First Black soloist at the Metropolitan Opera.</div>
      <div class="otd-born-more">+ 2 more born this day →</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
